## 4. Operational Flow (Simplified)

1. Member elects allocation percentage and asset mix (within approved limits) and agrees to the valuation, top-up and liquidation rules (Sections 3.5–3.6).
2. Assets are transferred to the trustee's SPV and held across at least two regulated custodians (Section 3.3).
3. Value and Coverage Ratio are calculated daily and shown on the member dashboard.
4. Once the recognised (post-haircut) value meets a threshold, the member can apply to participating lenders for a home loan that recognises the collateral.
5. On loan approval, the collateral is pledged under controlled conditions (from Phase 1 only, once the legal change in Section 7 is made).
6. If coverage falls, the bands, top-up calls and deadlines in Section 3.5 apply, followed if needed by staged de-risking (Section 3.6). Enforcement occurs only on loan default.
7. On loan repayment or sale of the property under approved circumstances, the pledge is released and the assets (or AUD proceeds) remain in the member's superannuation account.

